rom the first  chapter starts defending midoriya saying  that the other civilians are too  hysterical and that obviously deku  doesn't want to stay there resting  forever the old man continues stating  that because they are spectators the  civilians have gotten used to seeing all  might fighting and have forgotten that  heroes have a heart he says that after  the war many heroes gave up so those  that are left must have an unwavering  determination he ends his speech by  asking how long are we planning to stay  as mere spectators now what he said  about all might is so valid because  because all this time all might was  saving people with a smile on his face  and he never ever showed that he was  afraid you know there was every scenario  where all might actually uh was  vulnerable until camino so i think that  you know people still have to get used  to the idea of heroes being actually  human beings rather than these uh  invincible monsters that that they were  perceived as because of all might um and  yeah i think it's a valid statement the  civilian who opposed deku in the last  chapter says that some people were  calling him all for one's henchmen while  others were calling him the hero's  greatest weapon and he was confused by  those conflicting opinions he asks deku  if after resting at ue if he will be  able to return things back to normal and  decker replies saying that they will all  fight for it ectoplasm then goes outside  the ua barrier to meet endeavour hawks  and shoto who were just standing there  and i didn't mention this in my last  chapter review but endeavour's outfit  right now i don't know what he's trying  to do right now i guess he's trying to  be undercover or something but it looks  like he's a buff detective or something  like that but anyway ectoplasm asks them  if they heard of shaco's speech and  tells them that they need to come in  because they won't want to miss what's  happening in this moment endeavor is  blaming himself saying that 